Galzu is a tengu of [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], the sister of [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and one of three children of [[People/Adal|Adal]]. She worked alongside her grandmother, and was the most driven of the three. Her feathers are mostly black, with blue at the tips of the longer ones, and she never cared for pink bows.

She spent months talking with the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]] in [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]]. She argued with her father and stormed out of the roost, and for a long time was not seen again. Her disappearance came at the same time as a break-in at a Belvedere archival facility. Adal searched her room afterward and found nothing out of place but the group she had fallen in with, and he could not find her anywhere in the city.

She has since turned up aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], in Neweth, the town around the heart [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Tally|Tally]], one of four tengu who rarely leave one another's company. [[People/Egan Arithmites|Egan]] counts her among a later, more fervent wave of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]]'s followers, stronger than the first group and given more of the god's gifts.

She worked a rite to wake the dead Heart, pouring magic into it from the inner sanctum above, with a pack of summoned dog-things at her feet. She came ready to fight and could still cast where sound is killed, and she held out until she was beaten down. She is dying at the foot of the Heart now. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] means to take her alive and step into her mind rather than let her die.
